c infection with constitutional symptoms and neurological manifestations: less likely due to blast count elevation and pancytopenia pattern", "Endocrine crisis (e.g., adrenal insufficiency): no hypotension, electrolyte chaos, or other adrenal-specific findings", "Metastatic visceral mass syndrome: no localized mass or focal neurological deficit to support this", "Diabetic decompensation (e.g., hyperglycemic crisis): blood glucose (99 mg/dL) and labs do not support acute metabolic derangement", "Vitamin B12/folate deficiency: no macrocytosis or neurocutaneous findings to support this"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with blasts (57,500/mm³ with 35% blasts)", "Systemic urgency (visual changes + ataxia in diabetic with acute weight loss)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Diabetes association is more typical of lymphoid processes, slightly favoring B2 and reducing B1 plausibility."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Acute neurological findings without chronic phase markers make blast crisis less likely than more aggressive myeloid or lymphoid processes."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoma features weakens B2 but retains possibility given CNS infiltration potential."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"